.TH HMW-RELAY 1 "" "help-me-win" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hmw-relay \- relay for help-me-win self-hosted remote support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hmw-relay serve
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR addr ]
.RB [ \-\-state
.IR dir ]
.br
.B hmw-relay helper add
.I name
.RB [ \-\-display
.IR "display name" ]
.I key
.br
.B hmw-relay helper remove
.I name
.br
.B hmw-relay helper list
.br
.B hmw-relay client list
.br
.B hmw-relay client remove
.I fingerprint
.br
.B hmw-relay hostkey
.br
.B hmw-relay version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hmw-relay
is the SSH relay of help-me-win. Helpers and the people they help connect to
it on one port; it authenticates their Ed25519 keys and splices their
sessions. The screen and input run end to end over an inner SSH connection
that the relay cannot read.
.PP
.B serve
runs the relay, by default on
.BR :5938 .
The other commands change or show the state directory; a running relay picks
up changes within a second.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " addr"
Address to listen on, as host:port or :port.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " dir"
State directory with the host key, helpers and registered clients. Default:
.B $HMW_RELAY_STATE
if set, else the per-user data directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HMW_RELAY_STATE
Default state directory. The Debian service sets it to
.IR /var/lib/hmw-relay .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hmw-relayctl (8)
